# Docker sends the whole build context to the daemon before the build starts,
# and "COPY . ." puts whatever survives this file into the image.
# Docker does NOT read .gitignore. This file is separate and has to repeat it.

.venv/                  # the virtualenv. The image builds its own from requirements.txt
.git/                   # the entire history, usually the largest thing in a repo
__pycache__/            # compiled bytecode, rebuilt inside the image anyway
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/          # local test cache, meaningless in the image
.idea/                  # PyCharm settings
.vscode/

data/processed/         # pipeline OUTPUT. The image regenerates it; shipping it
                        # would bake yesterday's results into the image.

.env                    # secrets are passed at run time with -e or --env-file,
                        # never built into a layer, where they persist in history

*.md                    # docs do not change what the application does
.github/                # CI config runs on the runner, not inside the image

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   data/*.csv    the INPUT data, or the pipeline has nothing to read
#   requirements.txt, src/, testing/   the application and its tests
